.TH STDERR 3crunch "" "Crunch" "Crunch Library Manual"
.SH NAME
stderr \- Crunch standard error stream
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <stdio.h>
.PP
.B struct FILE* stderr;
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B stderr
is the initially open, unbuffered Crunch stream for file descriptor 2.
It can be passed to Crunch stream functions and closed with
.BR fclose (3crunch).
After closing it the stream pointer is invalid.
.SH NOTES
Crunch stream objects are not C library
.B FILE
objects. The standard stream names are macros referring to Crunch-specific
global pointers; they do not interoperate with libc's stream objects.
Mixing stream operations with direct descriptor operations requires care:
they share a descriptor, but not stream indicator state.
Crunch streams and errno are not thread-safe.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR stdin (3crunch),
.BR stdout (3crunch),
.BR fputc (3crunch),
.BR fclose (3crunch)
